Added Permission Policy, Policy Parameter, Policy Rule and Policy Assignment models: a reusable permission definition with named parameters, whose constraints are rendered at permission-check time instead of being stored as object permissions.
Added REST API endpoints for permission policies and assignments, including path resolution (`resolve-path/`), generated constraints (`constraints/`) and preview (`preview/`), plus `effective-access/` on the users endpoint.
Added permission policy, policy parameter, policy rule and policy assignment UI under Extensibility > Users; parameters and rules have their own pages and can also be edited in place on the policy form, and the rule form proposes lookup paths from the object type to each parameter.
Added a visual constraint editor (`ConstraintEditorField`) that builds permission constraints by browsing a model's fields and relations, and model-field introspection UI API endpoints backing it.
Added an effective-access page (Profile > Access) and an administrator view listing every grant a user holds from stored permissions and policy assignments, with the source of each.
Added a provisional `in_tree` ORM lookup for foreign keys to tree models (`location__in_tree`), matching a node and all of its descendants, usable in object permission constraints and policy templates. Its implementation is not yet ratified and may change before release.
Added built-in permission policies for tenant-scoped device access, reference-data viewing and export-job execution.
Added the `create_permission_policy_demo_data` management command, which creates demo users, groups, policies and assignments illustrating the permission policy patterns (development environments only).
Added the `hyperlinked_object_list` template tag, rendering links to a sample of objects with an "… and N more" tail linking to the full list.
Added a Preview tab to permission policies and policy assignments, showing per object type the rendered constraint, the match count and a sample, and a Generated constraints panel on assignments listing the equivalent object permission records with an optional "Definition (JSON)" column in the shape the object permissions REST API accepts.
Added warnings on the policy form, the assignment list and detail pages and the effective access page when an assignment lacks a value for a policy parameter, which makes the assignment grant nothing.
